ActivityManager: Let a device set the cached process limit and OOM update policy

Android 11 keeps up to 32 cached processes, which only the
activity_manager max_cached_processes flag can change. On the Echo Dot
(2nd gen) the six it cached held about 46 MB that MemAvailable never
counts. ro.config.max_cached_processes lets a device set a lower default.

A quick OOM adjustment skips trimming when a process stays cached, so an
empty process that went cached while still bound lived on until the next
full update, which an idle device rarely runs.
ro.config.oomadj_update_quick=false makes every update a full one. The
activity_manager flags still override both.

